WEBVTT

1
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:37.333
<b>Arjuna had asked Lord Krishna four questions </b>
<b>about an enlightened person (Sthitaprajna).</b>

2
00:00:37.333 --> 00:00:39.625
<b>Arjuna's fourth question was</b>

3
00:00:39.625 --> 00:00:43.500
<b>about how an enlightened </b>
<b>person conducts themselves</b>

4
00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:49.000
<b>specifically, how do they operate their senses?</b>

5
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:52.750
<b>This verse provides that answer.</b>

6
00:00:52.750 --> 00:00:58.958
<b>Lord Krishna says that one who maintains neither</b>
<b>attachment nor aversion to material objects, </b>

7
00:00:58.958 --> 00:01:01.750
<b>whose senses are naturally controlled,</b>

8
00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:04.708
<b>and whose mind is fully disciplined</b>

9
00:01:04.708 --> 00:01:06.958
<b>such an enlightened person</b>

10
00:01:06.958 --> 00:01:11.708
<b>even while living amidst worldly </b>
<b>affairs and sense objects,</b>

11
00:01:11.708 --> 00:01:15.208
<b>achieves purity and peace.</b>

12
00:01:20.166 --> 00:01:23.500
<b>In the previous verse, Krishna explained</b>

13
00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:31.791
<b>the harmful consequences of not protecting</b>
<b>our senses from worldly attachments.</b>

14
00:01:31.791 --> 00:01:35.916
<b>Naturally, this might raise </b>
<b>a question in your mind:</b>

15
00:01:35.916 --> 00:01:40.666
<b>when the world is full of sensory attractions,</b>

16
00:01:40.666 --> 00:01:45.208
<b>and we cannot avoid worldly duties,</b>

17
00:01:45.208 --> 00:01:47.250
<b>what should we do?</b>

18
00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:50.500
<b>How can we protect our senses?</b>

19
00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:52.833
<b>Here is the answer.</b>

20
00:01:52.833 --> 00:01:54.500
<b>Krishna explains</b>

21
00:01:54.500 --> 00:02:05.416
<b>that if we maintain neither attachment nor hatred </b>
<b>toward any sensory experience or object,</b>

22
00:02:05.416 --> 00:02:10.875
<b>and if we perform worldly</b>
<b>duties simply as activities,</b>

23
00:02:10.875 --> 00:02:16.458
<b>then we can operate our senses in the world.</b>

24
00:02:16.458 --> 00:02:18.875
<b>Think of it this way</b>

25
00:02:18.875 --> 00:02:20.291
<b>eating</b>

26
00:02:20.291 --> 00:02:22.583
<b>is a necessity of life,</b>

27
00:02:22.583 --> 00:02:26.791
<b>and while eating, the tongue remains active,</b>

28
00:02:26.791 --> 00:02:29.125
<b>experiencing taste.</b>

29
00:02:29.125 --> 00:02:32.666
<b>If a person controls this experience of taste</b>

30
00:02:32.666 --> 00:02:36.333
<b>and maintains no attachment to food,</b>

31
00:02:36.333 --> 00:02:41.291
<b>they will eat only as a vital life activity.</b>

32
00:02:41.291 --> 00:02:46.916
<b>They will consume only what is</b>
<b>necessary for bodily functions.</b>

33
00:02:46.916 --> 00:02:51.958
<b>Here, taste has no connection </b>
<b>with the quantity of food.</b>

34
00:02:51.958 --> 00:02:54.333
<b>This is what sensory control means.</b>

35
00:02:54.333 --> 00:02:55.333
<b>Similarly,</b>

36
00:02:55.333 --> 00:03:00.250
<b>if they need to take bitter medicine when ill,</b>

37
00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:03.000
<b>they won't be disturbed by it.</b>

38
00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:07.666
<b>It's a necessary activity for health improvement,</b>

39
00:03:07.666 --> 00:03:09.666
<b>and they will complete it.</b>

40
00:03:09.666 --> 00:03:12.666
<b>This will restore their health.</b>

41
00:03:12.666 --> 00:03:14.875
<b>The result of such controlled mind</b>

42
00:03:14.875 --> 00:03:21.916
<b>and regulated activities is what's called </b>
<b>"prasadam adhigacchati"</b>

43
00:03:21.916 --> 00:03:27.041
<b>the attainment of purity and mental peace.</b>

44
00:03:27.041 --> 00:03:29.208
<b>This verse is significant</b>

45
00:03:29.208 --> 00:03:33.166
<b>As while living amidst the </b>
<b>world and worldly activities,</b>

46
00:03:33.166 --> 00:03:37.125
<b>it illuminates certain principles to follow.</b>

47
00:03:37.125 --> 00:03:42.500
<b>It suggests a path to keep the senses </b>
<b>under control even while engaging them,</b>

48
00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:46.291
<b>showing the way to their protection.</b>

49
00:03:51.125 --> 00:03:59.291
<b>Can control or restriction</b>
<b>lead you towards freedom?</b>

50
00:03:59.291 --> 00:04:03.000
<b>This might sound paradoxical.</b>

51
00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:05.875
<b>But reflect again</b>

52
00:04:05.875 --> 00:04:11.250
<b>on how restrictions and </b>
<b>rules are created for your help,</b>

53
00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:16.500
<b>to protect you from harm.</b>

54
00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:22.625
<b>You must have seen a kite flying, </b>
<b>perhaps flown one yourself.</b>

55
00:04:22.625 --> 00:04:28.458
<b>Have you ever considered that </b>
<b>the string which controls the kite</b>

56
00:04:28.458 --> 00:04:33.000
<b>also gives it freedom,</b>

57
00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:36.833
<b>enables it to soar high in the sky?</b>

58
00:04:36.833 --> 00:04:40.958
<b>What happens if that string breaks?</b>

59
00:04:40.958 --> 00:04:44.416
<b>The kite will quickly fall to earth,</b>

60
00:04:44.416 --> 00:04:46.833
<b>damaged.</b>

61
00:04:46.833 --> 00:04:50.541
<b>No kite would ever want this.</b>

62
00:04:50.541 --> 00:04:52.750
<b>The string enables its flight.</b>

63
00:04:52.750 --> 00:04:56.958
<b>The kite's freedom lies in its control.</b>

64
00:04:56.958 --> 00:04:59.000
<b>Similarly,</b>

65
00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:04.125
<b>rules and restrictions are necessary</b>

66
00:05:04.125 --> 00:05:07.375
<b>for humans to soar high in life.</b>

67
00:05:07.375 --> 00:05:10.333
<b>You can understand it this way:</b>

68
00:05:10.333 --> 00:05:13.250
<b>you've set a goal,</b>

69
00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:17.666
<b>but a TV series deeply attracts you,</b>

70
00:05:17.666 --> 00:05:21.875
<b>and before you know it, your time is wasted.</b>

71
00:05:21.875 --> 00:05:25.291
<b>You drift away from your goal.</b>

72
00:05:25.291 --> 00:05:27.958
<b>In this case, were you free?</b>

73
00:05:27.958 --> 00:05:32.458
<b>Or were you bound by that series?</b>

74
00:05:32.458 --> 00:05:36.166
<b>But if you exercise self-control,</b>

75
00:05:36.166 --> 00:05:41.125
<b>restrict yourself from wasting time on that series,</b>

76
00:05:41.125 --> 00:05:44.791
<b>you become free from its influence.</b>

77
00:05:44.791 --> 00:05:51.958
<b>This self-control will help </b>
<b>guide you toward your goal.</b>

78
00:05:51.958 --> 00:05:57.125
<b>Without discipline, even a highly talented person</b>

79
00:05:57.125 --> 00:06:01.166
<b>remains unable to achieve greatness.</b>

80
00:06:01.166 --> 00:06:10.208
<b>When voluntarily embraced, control </b>
<b>and restrictions help unleash your talents.</b>

81
00:06:10.208 --> 00:06:14.291
<b>Don't become subservient to any desire or object</b>

82
00:06:14.291 --> 00:06:17.000
<b>that prevents you from soaring high.</b>

83
00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:21.875
<b>Make yourself independent</b>
<b>through disciplined living.</b>

84
00:06:26.208 --> 00:06:29.750
<b>It's often observed in society</b>

85
00:06:29.750 --> 00:06:31.250
<b>that youth</b>

86
00:06:31.250 --> 00:06:35.541
<b>dislike cultural restrictions.</b>

87
00:06:35.541 --> 00:06:42.625
<b>In their impulse, they sometimes </b>
<b>label such restrictions as mere orthodoxy.</b>

88
00:06:42.625 --> 00:06:51.000
<b>They begin to see these as obstacles to their</b>
<b>free expression, entertainment, and freedom.</b>

89
00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:51.958
<b>However,</b>

90
00:06:51.958 --> 00:06:54.375
<b>we often see</b>

91
00:06:54.375 --> 00:07:01.041
<b>that this illusion of freedom </b>
<b>transforms into indiscipline,</b>

92
00:07:01.041 --> 00:07:06.791
<b>becoming a source of major problems later in life.</b>

93
00:07:06.791 --> 00:07:08.666
<b>For example</b>

94
00:07:08.666 --> 00:07:14.083
<b>if someone receives excessive</b>
<b>freedom at a young age,</b>

95
00:07:14.083 --> 00:07:17.958
<b>if all restrictions are removed,</b>

96
00:07:17.958 --> 00:07:21.125
<b>there can be adverse consequences.</b>

97
00:07:21.125 --> 00:07:27.458
<b>They might lose discipline</b>
<b>and stray from their goals,</b>

98
00:07:27.458 --> 00:07:31.583
<b>or move towards bad company,</b>

99
00:07:31.583 --> 00:07:32.750
<b>and</b>

100
00:07:32.750 --> 00:07:43.375
<b>in many serious cases, we've seen </b>
<b>this lead to substance abuse and addiction.</b>

101
00:07:43.375 --> 00:07:46.958
<b>Then the same youth will regret,</b>

102
00:07:46.958 --> 00:07:52.416
<b>suffering the consequences </b>
<b>of so-called "free expression."</b>

103
00:07:52.416 --> 00:08:00.125
<b>Freedom never means the </b>
<b>absence of rules and restrictions.</b>

104
00:08:00.125 --> 00:08:04.833
<b>True freedom is that which </b>
<b>guides you on the right path,</b>

105
00:08:04.833 --> 00:08:08.875
<b>protects from harm, and instills </b>
<b>a sense of responsibility.</b>

106
00:08:08.875 --> 00:08:12.875
<b>Therefore, if you want to </b>
<b>give your family members</b>

107
00:08:12.875 --> 00:08:23.125
<b>and yourself a secure, joyful life, </b>
<b>certain restrictions will definitely help.</b>

108
00:08:23.125 --> 00:08:30.708
<b>Another adverse effect of lacking </b>
<b>restrictions and rules, visible nowadays,</b>

109
00:08:30.708 --> 00:08:37.083
<b>is addiction to entertainment</b>
<b>and communication media.</b>

110
00:08:37.083 --> 00:08:45.000
<b>If we self-impose restrictions </b>
<b>to save time wasted here,</b>

111
00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:50.208
<b>families can spend that</b>
<b>time in mutual conversation.</b>

112
00:08:50.208 --> 00:08:56.791
<b>This would be proper utilization of time, </b>
<b>deepening relationships.</b>

113
00:08:56.791 --> 00:09:03.541
<b>Restrictions are like the iron </b>
<b>fence around a garden,</b>

114
00:09:03.541 --> 00:09:09.875
<b>which protects flowers by </b>
<b>keeping harmful animals out,</b>

115
00:09:09.875 --> 00:09:13.416
<b>enhancing the garden's beauty.</b>

116
00:09:13.416 --> 00:09:21.333
<b>You too can secure and beautify </b>
<b>your garden of life using some rules.</b>

117
00:09:26.166 --> 00:09:35.541
<b>Sometimes people mistakenly equate complete </b>
<b>absence of restrictions with freedom.</b>

118
00:09:35.541 --> 00:09:41.791
<b>Another form of this appears in professional life,</b>

119
00:09:41.791 --> 00:09:49.958
<b>where sometimes people reject any </b>
<b>suggestion to change their working style.</b>

120
00:09:49.958 --> 00:09:52.583
<b>They proudly declare,</b>

121
00:09:52.583 --> 00:09:55.875
<b>"I prefer to remain free,</b>

122
00:09:55.875 --> 00:10:01.541
<b>I work according to myself alone, not others."</b>

123
00:10:01.541 --> 00:10:04.208
<b>This is certainly ego,</b>

124
00:10:04.208 --> 00:10:08.291
<b>but never freedom.</b>

125
00:10:08.291 --> 00:10:15.208
<b>Positive suggestions, and sometimes </b>
<b>even criticism, are necessary for everyone.</b>

126
00:10:15.208 --> 00:10:21.458
<b>Completely rejecting them </b>
<b>is blocking your own progress.</b>

127
00:10:21.458 --> 00:10:29.625
<b>Through reactions, suggestions, and criticisms, </b>
<b>humanity has made such progress,</b>

128
00:10:29.625 --> 00:10:32.583
<b>achieved such great inventions,</b>

129
00:10:32.583 --> 00:10:37.458
<b>made remarkable improvements.</b>

130
00:10:37.458 --> 00:10:42.375
<b>If suggestions and criticism bother you,</b>

131
00:10:42.375 --> 00:10:47.458
<b>try to keep these two points in mind:</b>

132
00:10:47.458 --> 00:10:49.041
<b>First</b>

133
00:10:49.041 --> 00:10:51.583
<b>No one here is perfect,</b>

134
00:10:51.583 --> 00:10:55.083
<b>all are on the path of improvement.</b>

135
00:10:55.083 --> 00:10:56.208
<b>Second</b>

136
00:10:56.208 --> 00:11:00.541
<b>Don't take criticism as a personal attack.</b>

137
00:11:00.541 --> 00:11:05.000
<b>It could be a good sign for improvement</b>

138
00:11:05.000 --> 00:11:06.375
<b>And finally,</b>

139
00:11:06.375 --> 00:11:11.583
<b>view others' reactions beyond like-dislike.</b>

140
00:11:11.583 --> 00:11:14.250
<b>Reflect with a calm mind.</b>

141
00:11:14.250 --> 00:11:19.333
<b>Implement what seems useful.</b>

